   NOTICE

   This sub-project ("ebics-mock-server") is **independent in-house code**,
   written from scratch by Orange Octo / Paperclip Treasury Engineering for
   the Orange Octo EBICS-3.0 PoC (issue ORA-2303). It is *not* a fork of
   any upstream EBICS implementation. No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was copied,
   adapted, or linked into this module.

   Specifically, this module does **not** derive from:
     - Libeufin / GNU Taler  (AGPL-3.0)
     - ebics-java-client     (LGPL-2.1)  — only consumed by the *sidecar*
     - JOONIS Python Fintech (commercial)
     - any other EBICS server, sandbox, or test harness

   Its sole purpose is to serve canned, deterministic responses to a small
   subset of EBICS-3.0 order types (HEV, INI, HIA, HPB, HKD, STA/C53, CCT)
   so that the production-target sidecar's smoke can be exercised without
   relying on an external bank sandbox.

   The Apache-2.0 license above applies to **this directory only**
   (treasury-poc/services/ebics-mock-server/). The rest of the
   rechnungstool repository is governed by the company's standard
   proprietary license.
